<title>USA: Ohio wheat crop good but in danger of freezing.</title>
<headline>Ohio wheat crop good but in danger of freezing.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ohio's winter wheat crop was entering winter in mostly good condition, but a substantial portion will be susceptible to extended periods of extremely cold temperatures, according to the latest crop report from the state's agricultural statistics service.</p>
<p>Soybean harvest was complete on 99 percent of the acreage during the week ended Sunday, just short of the five-year average of 100 percent, the report said.</p>
<p>Corn harvesting reached 85 percent complete. That pace compared with the five-year average of 92 percent.</p>
<p>There were five days suitable for fieldwork.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-983-7347))</p>
</text>
